<title>USA: Charter Communications Q1 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Charter Communications Q1 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1st Qtr	 4th Qtr     1st Qtr</p>
<p>					1997	    1996	  1996</p>
<p> Revenues		   $ 2,749,356    $2,927,370   $ 431,722</p>
<p> Net Loss		  ( 2,540,619)  ( 4,071,873)  ( 707,652)</p>
<p> Net Loss Per Share	   ( 0.09)	 ( 0.17)     ( 0.09)</p>
<p>Shares Used in Computing</p>
<p>  Net Loss Per Share     27,836,826    24,108,005   8,282,932</p>
<p>NOTE:  Charter Communications International Inc said its net income for the first quarter of 1997 was adversely impacted by a one time loss on extinguishment of subordinated debentures of approximately $242,000, as well as approximately $500,000 in non-recurring expenses primarily due to a delay in the re-engineering of Charter's long distance network.</p>
<p>During the first quarter, the company completed a private placement which added 2.5 million shares of common stock.</p>
